Mechanical properties\par
\par
    Bulk modulus: Ratio of pressure to volumetric compression (GPa)\par
    Coefficient of friction (also depends on surface finish)\par
    Coefficient of restitution\par
    Compressive strength: stress a material can withstand before compressive failure (MPa)\par
    Creep: the slow and gradual deformation of an object with respect to time\par
    Ductility: Ability of a material to deform under tensile load (% elongation)\par
    Fatigue limit: Maximum stress a material can withstand under repeated loading (MPa)\par
    Flexural modulus\par
    Flexural strength\par
    Fracture toughness: Energy absorbed by unit area before the fracture of material (J/m^2)\par
    Hardness: Ability to withstand surface indentation (e.g. Brinnell hardness number)\par
    Plasticity: Ability of a material to undergo irreversible deformations (-)\par
    Poisson's ratio: Ratio of lateral strain to axial strain (no units)\par
    Resilience: Ability of a material to absorb energy when it is deformed elastically (M Pa)\par
    Shear modulus: Ratio of shear stress to shear strain (M Pa)\par
    Shear strain: in the angle between two perpendicular lines in a plane\par
    Shear strength: Maximum shear stress a material can withstand\par
    Specific modulus: Modulus per unit volume (M Pa/ m^3)\par
    Specific strength: Strength per unit density (Nm/kg)\par
    Specific weight: Weight per unit volume (N/m^3)\par
    Surface roughness\par
    Tensile strength: Maximum tensile stress a material can withstand before failure (MPa)\par
    Yield strength: The stress at which a material starts to yield (MPa)\par
    Young's modulus: Ratio of linear stress to linear strain (MPa)\par
